---
import "../styles/global.css";

export const prerender = false;

const { user } = Astro.locals;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png" />
    <title>10x Study Planner</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Turns a topic list, a deadline and a weekly time budget into a dated study plan, and keeps it honest as life interferes."
    />
  </head>
  <body class="min-h-screen bg-slate-50 text-slate-900 antialiased">
    <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:py-24">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">10x Study Planner</h1>

      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-slate-600">
        You know what you have to cover before the exam. What you decide badly, at the end of a long day, is
        <em>when</em>. This works that out for you.
      </p>

      <section class="mt-10 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide text-slate-500 uppercase">How it works</h2>
        <ol class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-slate-700">
          <li>
            <span class="font-medium text-slate-900">1.</span> List your topics with an estimate, a priority and an optional
            deadline.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-medium text-slate-900">2.</span> Say how many minutes you really have on each weekday. Zero
            is allowed, and respected.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-medium text-slate-900">3.</span> Generate the week. Each evening gets filled, never past what
            you declared.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-medium text-slate-900">4.</span> Mark sessions done or skipped. The next plan is built from
            what actually happened.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-6 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide text-slate-500 uppercase">How it decides</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">
          Each topic is scored by the daily pace it would need to finish on time, weighted by how much it matters. A
          deadline that is close therefore beats a topic that is merely important, and because urgency falls as work
          gets done, topics under similar pressure take turns instead of one of them swallowing the week.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        {
          user ? (
            <a
              href="/dashboard"
              class="rounded-md bg-slate-900 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-white transition-colors hover:bg-slate-700"
            >
              Open this week
            </a>
          ) : (
            <>
              <a
                href="/auth/signup"
                class="rounded-md bg-slate-900 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-white transition-colors hover:bg-slate-700"
              >
                Create an account
              </a>
              <a
                href="/auth/signin"
                class="rounded-md border border-slate-300 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 transition-colors hover:bg-slate-100"
              >
                Sign in
              </a>
            </>
          )
        }
      </div>

      <footer class="mt-16 border-t border-slate-200 pt-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
        Course project for 10xDevs 3.0. Source and design notes on
        <a href="https://github.com/Ariowistus/10x-study-planner" class="underline hover:text-slate-900">GitHub</a>.
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
